module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.absence_classifier_default_bucket

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data absence_classifier_default_bucket: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "absence_classifier_default_bucket" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**absence-classifier default bucket, unprotected by its residual refusal** (a classifier whose ACCEPTED bucket is defined by the ABSENCE of properties is only as complete as the enumeration of kinds it was derived from, and it fails silently TOWARD THE DEFAULT rather than toward its refusal arm.",

    "The refusal reads as coverage and is not: a residual can only catch kinds whose absence PATTERN differs from the accepted one, which is a strictly smaller population than the kinds that exist.",

    "SPECIMEN IN A COMPLETION PREDICATE, TWICE IN ONE HOUR BY TWO AUTHORS (2026-09-04). A CI watch used all(.bucket != \"pending\") as its terminal test -- an accepted bucket defined by the absence of the single known REJECTING value, so every unmodeled value lands in acceptance: an error shape, a rate-limit body, a decode failure, a renamed future state. It reported ALL TERMINAL while both subject runs were still queued, because the gh path had begun failing against an exhausted GitHub App installation token. That exhaustion was invisible in the author's own rate_limit, which showed healthy core and graphql budgets, since the throttled quota belonged to the installation rather than the token. A second session shipped the same defect independently in the same hour with a different surface -- exit condition \"no pending in the output\", against an API returning an error instead of any buckets. Both authors had written about this class shortly before.",

    "THE OBVIOUS REPAIR OPENS THE DUAL CLASS, WHICH IS THE PART WORTH CARRYING: replacing the negation with a positive allowlist and routing everything else to KEEP WAITING converts this row's defect into unhandled_state_falls_to_the_not_yet_arm -- a settled state the fold does not recognise becomes indistinguishable from a subject still progressing, and waiting can never resolve it because the subject already finished. Measured on the first repair: the seven-conclusion allowlist omitted RunStale and RunStartupFailure, both present in the modeled vocabulary at extdeps.github.actions_runs, so the rearmed watch would have held forever on either. A closed accepting set is necessary and is NOT sufficient.",

    "THE SUFFICIENT SHAPE NEEDS FOUR DISJOINT OUTPUTS WHERE BOTH FAILED VERSIONS HAD TWO -- settled with a modeled conclusion, subject still progressing, observation refused (transport, token, decode: repair the instrument rather than poll it), and conclusion unknown (a settled but unmodeled spelling: stop and escalate the vocabulary). An expired installation token is an observation refusal and not a run state; an unrecognised conclusion is not still-queued. Neither may be represented as subject progress. And a positive allowlist still passes VACUOUSLY over an empty population, since all([]) holds -- so the fold must also join against the expected subject manifest and report incomplete coverage rather than completion when zero records come back for a nonempty expectation.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: A RESIDUAL REFUSAL DOES NOT PROTECT A CLASSIFIER WHOSE ACCEPTED BUCKET IS DEFINED BY ABSENCE; A NEW KIND CAN SILENTLY RESEMBLE THE DEFAULT.",

    "THE CLASS HAS NOW PRODUCED BOTH POLARITIES FROM ONE CLASSIFIER, which is what makes it structural rather than anecdotal.",

    "v1.compiler.parse decided 'this module item is a type declaration' from no body AND no transport AND no type annotation.",

    "OVER-STAMPING: `resource Filesystem` / `Clock` / `Entropy` in std.resources carry none of those three, so all three were stamped TYPE DECLARATIONS -- and the exhaustive match's ModuleItemUnrecognized arm could not fire, because a resource is not unrecognised, it is INDISTINGUISHABLE from a type under that rule.",

    "The premise that the item kinds were four was falsified by the parser's own item error, which names ten: alias, type, fn, func, service, resource, data, extern, pattern, interface.",

    "UNDER-STAMPING: the repair keyed the resource arm on `properties` being non-empty, and `type X sole_constructor { ..",

    "}` carries a property too -- so 202 sole-constructor type declarations across 100 modules were classified as RESOURCES and vanished from the declaration population.",

    "Opposite direction, same classifier, same root: an absence-and-presence heuristic standing where a positive kind belongs.",

    "WHY EXCLUSION-BY-NAME IS NOT THE FIX EITHER, though it is what stands today: the surviving repair excludes the ONE modifier the minting authority owns, and it is complete by ENUMERATION OF MINTING SITES rather than by grep -- v1.compiler.parse has exactly two, parsed_sole_constructor_properties (one field-init named sole_constructor, the only source every type-item constructor passes along) and parse_resource_entries; nominal_opaque is dropped lexically by drop_leading_type_modifier and mints nothing; mint_parsed_optional_int_property is confined to nested where-predicate nodes.",

    "A one-member set established by construction is worth more than a longer list found by search.",

    "But a second modifier that MINTS a property on a type item reintroduces this in the same silent direction, and no longer list can prevent that.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability and not an artifact: parse constructors that CARRY the module-item kind they already dispatched on, consumed by an exhaustive match with NO DEFAULT TYPE BUCKET -- at which point membership is decided at construction and the residual refusal becomes real rather than decorative.",

    "THE SECOND SPECIMEN IS IN A DIFFERENT AUTHORITY AND IS FILED, NOT REPAIRED: v1.compiler.emit_core_support is_leaf_type_item, then named is_bare_leaf_item, read a CAPABILITY-LESS resource as a type declaration -- `resource Network` and `resource AuthContext` in std.resources have no children, no body, no params and no connective -- so the emit-side shape predicates carry the same defect in the same direction.",

    "Two specimens, one module, unrepaired here because it is a change to a different authority and smuggling it into a parser change would fork the subject.",

    "A THIRD SPECIMEN, IN A THIRD AUTHORITY, FILED AND NOT REPAIRED (2026-09-08) -- and it arrives with a REFINEMENT of this row's recognition rule rather than a second row. `v1.compiler.infer declared_type_inhabitance` decides a PAIR rather than classifying one subject, and its arms enumerate the ways two types can be RELATED: one refinement chain nesting inside the other, or the two chains MEETING on a shared link. A pair whose chains share NOTHING matches no arm, falls through the whole procedure, and is ADMITTED. Measured: `HostIdentity` (declared `NonEmptyStr where brand(...)`) passed at a formal declared as an ordinary product reaches no refusal at the direct call argument seam.",

    "IT IS THIS CLASS AND NOT A NEW ONE, AND THE GROUNDING IS A SHARED CAUSAL PREDICATE RATHER THAN A RESEMBLANCE. What both specimens instantiate is one cause: AN ACCEPTING RESIDUAL DEFINED BY `NO EXPLICIT ARM MATCHED`, so a member of the declared subject population that no arm dispositions silently lands in acceptance. That is the mechanism named at the head of this row, stated at the grain that makes it checkable. Arity changes none of it -- whether the question ranges over one subject or over a pair, the residual is still defined by what did not match rather than by what the subject IS, and the escaping population is still whatever the enumerated arms failed to reach. NO UNIVERSAL LAW IS BEING INVOKED HERE, and an earlier draft of this paragraph invoked one -- `two things that share a mechanism and a repair are one class` -- which is not true in general and was doing the work the causal predicate should do: a shared repair is EVIDENCE about the cause and never the argument for the fold. The argument is the cause; the repair is downstream of it.",

    "WHAT IS GENUINELY NEW, AND IT IS A RECOGNITION RULE THIS ROW DID NOT CARRY: RECOGNITION RULE -- WHERE THE DOMAIN IS ORDERED BY SEVERITY AND THE ENUMERATED ARMS COVER ONLY THE NEAR END, THE ACCEPTING RESIDUAL IS THE FAR END, AND SAFETY THEN RUNS BACKWARDS ALONG THAT ORDER. STATED AS A CONDITIONAL CONSEQUENCE AND NOT AS A MONOTONICITY THEOREM: this row does not claim that severity and admission are monotonically related in general, and does not claim the order is even total. It claims that WHEN the arms happen to enumerate the near end of a severity order, THEN the far end is what falls through -- which is a consequence of which cases were written, not a law about incompatibility. It is a TELL to check for, not a property to rely on. This is NOT derivable from the rule above: `A NEW KIND CAN SILENTLY RESEMBLE THE DEFAULT` predicts that UNMODELED kinds land in acceptance, and says nothing about an ordering being inverted. Here the escaping population is not a kind nobody enumerated and might arrive later -- it is present, well defined, and known at authoring time. Pairs that merely MEET are reported undecidable and are therefore located and countable; the wholly unrelated pair, the stronger incompatibility on this order this specimen exhibits, is accepted outright.",

    "THE TELL, and it is the most transferable thing in this specimen because it is a review instruction rather than a code smell: READ THE PROCEDURE'S EXITS, NOT ITS ARMS. A decision procedure whose fallthrough is admission looks complete to anyone auditing the cases it handles, because every handled case is handled correctly. Ask instead what happens to an input no arm claims, and whether that answer is a DECISION or a DEFAULT.",

    "ATTRIBUTION, MEASURED ON BOTH SIDES RATHER THAN ACCEPTED FROM THE FINDING THAT RAISED IT. The specimen was surfaced by a review of gunbc#10727, which attributed it to a where-refinement exclusion that PR added to the nominal-product arm. THAT ATTRIBUTION DOES NOT SURVIVE MEASUREMENT: the same control over the same fixtures and corpus, run against two compilers differing only in the three stage0 infer mirrors, returns false under BOTH. Removing the exclusion does not change the result, because the product arm was not making the refusal the exclusion was thought to suppress. The finding's CONCLUSION was right and its CAUSE was not, which is why this receipt records the mechanism rather than the review's account of it, and why the specimen is filed here rather than as a defect of that PR.",

    "RUNG FOR THIS SPECIMEN: below the ladder -- silent wrongness, a value of an unrelated constructor ACCEPTED at a declared position with no diagnostic in either direction. CEILING: 3 (structurally guaranteed): both sides' identities are decidable here, each resolving to a declaration carrying a refinement chain, so a procedure that reaches a TOTAL decision over the pair refuses this from modeled structure rather than validating it afterwards. What stands between the specimen and its ceiling is not decidability but the absence of a total exit. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER for it, at CAPABILITY grain: the declared-type inhabitance judgment's FINAL DEFAULT stops accepting. `Inhabits` for an identity-established pair requires a NAMED POSITIVE COMPATIBILITY AUTHORITY -- there is no implicit accepting residual -- sufficient for the `HostIdentity`-at-`Box` specimen to refuse. THE GRAIN IS DELIBERATE AND THE OBVIOUS PHRASING IS WRONG: a trigger reading `refuses every pair whose refinement chains are disjoint` is BROADER THAN THE DEFECT and would license an OVER-REFUSING repair, since disjointness is not itself evidence of incompatibility. The defect is the accepting residual at the final default, so that is what the trigger names. Neither a control existing nor a diagnostic variant being declared retires it, since both would be satisfied while the capability stayed dead.",

    "EVIDENCE FOR THIS SPECIMEN, EXECUTED AND ENROLLED: `test.claim.declared_type_inhabitance_direct_call_witness.w_a_branded_refinement_at_an_unrelated_product_formal_still_refuses`, admitted `ExpectAssertionFalse` so the RED executes and is HELD rather than blocking. Per DESIGN section 4b(4) it does not retire when the wall lands -- it flips to a permanent regression control.",

    "THE COUNTERMEASURE, AND IT IS THE MOST TRANSFERABLE THING IN THIS ROW: those two were invisible while ONE classifier answered, because both readers of the question AGREED they were types -- the agreed-wrong pair a disagreement census cannot see by construction ([[disagreement_census_blind_to_agreed_wrong]]), and no amount of running that census harder finds it.",

    "Splitting the question across two INDEPENDENTLY DERIVED readers -- absence-of-body/transport/annotation in the parser versus connective/params/children in the emitter -- converted their agreement into a disagreement, which is the only form the census can report.",

    "That split arrived here as a side effect of building the population join, not as a design goal, which is exactly why it is written down: RECOGNITION RULE: WHERE A CENSUS COMPARES TWO READERS, A THIRD INDEPENDENTLY-DERIVED READER IS THE ONLY THING THAT CAN FALSIFY THEIR AGREEMENT -- reach for it ON PURPOSE when an agreed-wrong population is suspected.",

    "The corpus-wide instrument is `type_occurrence_binding_census --establish`, joining the two readers at occurrence-id grain with uniqueness on both sides and no extra members.)",

    "THE TRIGGER FIRED, 2026-09-04. The parse constructors now CARRY the kind: v1.std.core Node has module_item_kind: ParsedModuleItemKind, stamped by the eight item constructors in v1.compiler.parse from the ItemForm body_kind they were already dispatching on, propagated at every construction that rebuilds a node, and consumed by an EXHAUSTIVE MATCH in all three emitters. Membership is decided at construction; there is no default type bucket to fall into; and the residual is now two named arms -- ModuleItemUnrecognized and NotAModuleItem -- that refuse in every target rather than a shape no one claimed. The second specimen this row filed and did not repair is repaired by the same motion: the emit-side predicates that decided an item's KIND from absence are deleted, and the four that survive decide TYPE STRUCTURE only, each gated on the carried kind.",

    "WHAT THE CLIMB COVERS AND WHAT IT DOES NOT, because the rung is the MINIMUM across the paths. The CLASSIFICATION axis reaches structurally impossible: no item can acquire a kind it was not constructed with, and a new ParsedModuleItemKind variant fails to compile at every dispatcher. The PAYLOAD axis does not move: Node is one carrier for items and expressions, so body and type_annotation stay optional and a kind-stamped item with a missing payload is still authorable. That residue is its own row, [[kind_carried_but_its_fields_stay_optional]], with the per-kind item carrier named as its trigger. Reporting the classification climb as if it closed both would be the rung inflation this ledger exists to catch.",

    "EVIDENCE, EXECUTED AND ENROLLED: v1.tests.claim.item_kind_dissolves_shape_predicates_control_test carries the discriminating RED -- a node satisfying every conjunct of the old shape test while carrying ModuleItemResource, which the shape-only predicate claimed and the kind-gated one refuses -- beside the accepted positive control that stops it being satisfied by a predicate that answers false for everything. Per DESIGN section 4b(4) both stay enrolled now that the machinery they falsified is deleted.",

    "AUDITED AGAINST [[required_evidence_absent_reads_as_evidence_of_pass]] AND FOUND DISTINCT RATHER THAN ASSUMED SO, because those two are the closest pair in the absence family and both present as accept-on-no-rejecting-observation. THE DISCRIMINATOR IS WHETHER THE ENUMERATION IS SHORT. Here it is OPEN -- an unmodeled kind exists and adding it is the repair, which is exactly the climb this row records. There it is CLOSED AND CORRECT: the required check is named in the roster and configured, and the admitted state is the EMPTY enumeration inside the demand-to-arrival window, where nothing is missing from the vocabulary at all. Carrying the kind at construction, the repair that took this row to structural, would leave that gate admitting unchanged. The family axis and the full membership are carried once, in [[absent_reads_identically_to_never_looked]].",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
